  "statusPaneNote": "⏳️ The PROGRESS half of the same status contract, beyond the cancel affordance above: what a World3d surface's compute-status pane says while an evaluation resolves. `visible` is React's own `WorldComputeStatusPane` gate (`computing || cancellable || phase === \"cancelled\"`) — a settled producer annotates nothing. `phaseLabel` is the producer's own `{en, de}` pair and is honoured only when BOTH tongues carry text; a renderer with no pair falls back to its own bilingual `common.loading`, never to the other language. `progressText` is `unitsDone/unitsTotal (percent%)` and is null for an indeterminate producer, whose bar paints a bare track rather than a lie. The Rust law answers through `world3d_compute_status`/`world3d_status_pill_for`, the TypeScript twin through `world3dComputeStatusV1`.",
