  "progressTimelineNote": "⏳️⛓️ ONE long preview evaluation, frame by frame, as the producer publishes it and as a surface must be able to show it. The law is the TIMELINE, not the row: at least four consecutive frames are non-idle, their ratio never decreases, the last frame is settled again, and every non-idle frame both paints a pill and offers the cancel the producer names. A run that publishes `idle` throughout satisfies every single-row assertion and is exactly the defect this section exists to fail — on both renderers the whole of a 23 s evaluation published `phase:\"idle\" inFlight:0 ratio:1.0` (ticket 26/09/09/PROCEDURAL-3D-END-TO-END, `📓️wgpu-progress-visibility-2026-09-14.md`). Language-neutral: the Rust law answers it through `world3d_compute_status`/`world3d_status_pill_for`, the TypeScript twin through `world3dComputeStatusV1` (`🔨️modules/🖱️ui/🎬️scene/🟦️.ts`), and the generation3d producer law proves its own projection emits exactly this shape.",
